<article class="env-lemma" id="07D2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07D2">Lemma <span data-tag="07D2">15.34.4</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. If $R[x_1, \ldots , x_ n]/(f_1, \ldots , f_ c)$ is a relative global complete intersection, then $f_1, \ldots , f_ c$ is a Koszul regular sequence. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Recall that the homology groups $H_ i(K_\bullet (f_\bullet ))$ are annihilated by the ideal $(f_1, \ldots , f_ c)$. Hence it suffices to show that $H_ i(K_\bullet (f_\bullet ))_\mathfrak q$ is zero for all primes $\mathfrak q \subset R[x_1, \ldots , x_ n]$ containing $(f_1, \ldots , f_ c)$. This follows from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00SV" data-tag="00SV">10.136.12</a> and the fact that a regular sequence is Koszul regular (Lemma <a href="/tag/062F" data-tag="062F">15.31.2</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>